/-!
# Marked higher quotient constructions in MS93

The central commutator constructs the single dual section (4.5.4)(v) from
the genuine doubled natural moving section (iv), the preceding (4.4) inputs,
and the literal (4.5.3)(i) equality. Its exact relative kernel, surjectivity,
and conjugation equation use CommonFacts.natural.marking and source.projection.
The resulting witness feeds the existing (4.5.5) commutator-layer assembly.

The doubled dual quotient (iii) and the doubled natural quotient (iv) still
need their source constructions. No existence of either pair model is
asserted here, and the contrary-assumption natural section from (4.3) is
not used to supply Earlier.natural_section.

Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher (1993), printed pp.898--899.
-/
